      "description": "Watch San Lorenzo vs Gimnasia M. highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 29, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina delivered a gripping encounter on July 29, 2026, as San Lorenzo hosted Gimnasia Mendoza . The match was a masterclass in tactical patience, with both sides searching for a way to break the deadlock under the watchful eyes of a passionate crowd. Tactical Maneuvers and Physicality After a scoreless opening forty-five minutes, the second half began with a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked to seize control. San Lorenzo introduced Cristian Nahuel Barrios at the restart, while Gimnasia Mendoza brought on Lautaro Carrera and Juan Rattalino . The increased pace led to a more physical contest, with yellow cards being handed out to Matias Recalde , Julian Ceballos , and Luciano Cingolani as the tension mounted across the pitch. The Final Breakthrough The game’s defining moment arrived in the 86th minute, sparked by the vision of substitute Gregorio Rodriguez . Having entered the pitch in the 59th minute, Rodriguez provided a pinpoint assist for Rodrigo Auzmendi , who clinical finishing found the back of the net to change the course of the evening. The goal sent the home supporters into a frenzy, rewarding their patience in what had been a stubbornly even contest. Seeing Out the Result In the aftermath of the goal, the match remained heated, with Facundo Lencioni receiving a yellow card in the 86th minute. To protect the lead, Guzman Corujo was brought on in the 89th minute to reinforce the defensive line. Despite late pressure, the structure held firm until the final whistle, concluding a match where strategic changes and a late surge of energy proved to be the difference-makers."
